# f1 = sum, f2 = target, f3 = forwards, f11 = wrap, f4 = sliced, f12 = drive, f5 = shape, f6 = relay, f7 = handsOn, f8 = byName, f9 = byKey, f10 = mapped, f13 = driveRoads
# A function of sloppy code that names `arguments` takes itself along: the object holds it under the name `callee`. It holds it as it holds anything else: whoever reads that name, or any name, or gets hold of the object, gets the function; a read under a number, `length`, and what apply and slice.call take out of the list do not.
# So such a function is followed like any other: Link knows its callers, and the walk copies its body into them: nothing of the four is left in the loop of drive(): no call, no list, no arguments object.
# RUN(LINK): link functions mechanisms=all
# LINK: function f1 callers-known
# RUN(COPIED): walk f12 mechanisms=all
# COPIED-LABEL: code f12:Body
# COPIED-NOT: CallDirect
# COPIED-NOT: CreateMappedArguments
# COPIED-NOT: NewArray
# A function that reaches its parameters through the object is walked in its own unit, as before.
# RUN(MAPPED): walk f13 mechanisms=all
# MAPPED-LABEL: code f13:Body
# MAPPED: function=f10
# Each road to the callee calls it with a text where the callers in sight hand it a number.
# RUN: run-in-shell
# CHECK: 50
# CHECK-NEXT: 54 8
# CHECK-NEXT: 2,text relayed,2,text by name,2,text by key,2
# CHECK-NEXT: 3,text relayed,3,text by name,3,text by key,3
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CHECKED): run-in-shell testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime
# CHECKED: 50
# CHECKED-NEXT: 54 8
# CHECKED-NEXT: 2,text relayed,2,text by name,2,text by key,2
# CHECKED-NEXT: 3,text relayed,3,text by name,3,text by key,3
# CHECKED-NEXT: exited with 0
